{
  "$schema-note": "Hand-maintained DATA, not code. Nothing under src/ imports it; two suites READ it.",
  "purpose": [
    "One sequence of OutboxEventStore calls and the transcript it must produce,",
    "run twice: against the in-memory double in this package, and against the",
    "real PostgreSQL store in packages/adapters/postgres-tenancy. ADR M0.3 §5.1",
    "rule (j2) forbids either adapter importing the other, so the two halves",
    "cannot share a module — and two independently written suites would measure",
    "two things and agree by coincidence. The CALLS and the EXPECTED TRANSCRIPT",
    "are therefore this file, and each package holds a small runner over it.",
    "",
    "Every row is spelled out: fixed identifiers, fixed instants, fixed bodies.",
    "Nothing in a transcript depends on a clock, on a random draw, or on which",
    "store answered — the environment identifiers are the one exception and are",
    "named by KEY here and mapped to seeded rows by each runner.",
    "",
    "THE STEP THIS FILE EXISTS FOR is `rollback-loses-the-appended-event`.",
    "`conversations` shipped a TestOutbox that was not in its unit of work's",
    "snapshot set, so an event appended inside a rolled-back transaction",
    "SURVIVED and certified a turn as settled against a settlement that never",
    "landed. Every test was green. Here the rejected transaction's first row is",
    "asked for immediately afterwards, from both stores, and both must have",
    "forgotten it."
  ],
